From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:07:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Clear the Pulse-Eight message queue without the adapter's
 lock held

The thread of CCECAdapterMessageQueue holds the queue's lock while it
writes a message, and CUSBCECAdapterCommunication::WriteToDevice() then
takes the adapter's lock. Close() did it the other way round: it held the
adapter's lock while it cleared the queue, which takes the queue's lock.
A message that reaches the queue's thread as Close() takes its lock (the
ping that the adapter is sent every 15 seconds, when it was queued just
before the reader stopped) leaves both waiting for each other, and the
close, and with it Kodi's standby or exit, hangs. The window is short,
but nothing ends the wait once it is entered.

Close() now takes the adapter's lock for the part that needs it, clears
the queue, which stops its thread, without it, and takes it again for the
rest. The order of what Close() does does not change.

Tests (outside the tree): libCEC built on the host with ThreadSanitizer,
opened and closed through a Pulse-Eight adapter emulated on a pseudo
terminal (a lock order inversion between the adapter and its message
queue before, none after).
---
 .../USBCECAdapterCommunication.cpp            | 27 ++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/libcec/adapter/Pulse-Eight/USBCECAdapterCommunication.cpp b/src/libcec/adapter/Pulse-Eight/USBCECAdapterCommunication.cpp
index c60b87c..6328f8a 100644
--- a/src/libcec/adapter/Pulse-Eight/USBCECAdapterCommunication.cpp
+++ b/src/libcec/adapter/Pulse-Eight/USBCECAdapterCommunication.cpp
@@ -214,24 +214,31 @@ void CUSBCECAdapterCommunication::Close(void)
   /* stop the reader thread */
   StopThread(0);
 
-  CLockObject lock(m_mutex);
-
-  /* set the ackmask to 0 before closing the connection */
-  if (IsOpen() && m_port->GetErrorNumber() == 0)
   {
-    LIB_CEC->AddLog(CEC_LOG_DEBUG, "%s - closing the connection", __FUNCTION__);
-    cec_logical_addresses addresses; addresses.Clear();
-    SetLogicalAddresses(addresses);
-    if (m_commands->GetFirmwareVersion() >= 2)
-      SetControlledMode(false);
+    CLockObject lock(m_mutex);
+
+    /* set the ackmask to 0 before closing the connection */
+    if (IsOpen() && m_port->GetErrorNumber() == 0)
+    {
+      LIB_CEC->AddLog(CEC_LOG_DEBUG, "%s - closing the connection", __FUNCTION__);
+      cec_logical_addresses addresses; addresses.Clear();
+      SetLogicalAddresses(addresses);
+      if (m_commands->GetFirmwareVersion() >= 2)
+        SetControlledMode(false);
+    }
   }
 
   /* the queue is only created by Open(), and Close() also runs on adapters that
      never got that far - a connection abandoned before the first open attempt,
-     or the destructor of one that failed to open */
+     or the destructor of one that failed to open.
+     it is cleared without m_mutex held: its thread holds the queue's lock while it
+     writes, and WriteToDevice() then takes m_mutex, so clearing it (which takes the
+     queue's lock) under m_mutex could wait forever for a write that had begun */
   if (m_adapterMessageQueue)
     m_adapterMessageQueue->Clear();
 
+  CLockObject lock(m_mutex);
+
   /* stop and delete the write thread */
   if (m_eepromWriteThread)
     m_eepromWriteThread->Stop();
